        "location": "Datong",
        "attractions": [
          {
            "name_base": "Huayan Temple (华严寺)",
            "name_local": "大同华严寺",
            "location_base": "Huayan Street, Ancient City Area, Datong, Shanxi",
            "location_local": "山西省大同市古城区华严寺街",
            "coordinates": {
              "lat": 40.092312,
              "lng": 113.286475
            },
            "cost": 65,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Liao Dynasty Buddhist Temple",
            "type_local": "辽代佛教寺院",
            "notes_base": "PRIORITY 1 city attraction — full day Datong Ancient City walk starts here. One of China's most important Liao dynasty (916-1125 AD) Buddhist temples. Contains the Daxiong Baodian (Great Hero Treasure Hall) — the largest surviving Liao-period Buddhist hall in China — and the Bojia Jiaocang Lou (1038 AD), a wooden scripture library with extraordinary cabinet carvings including the celebrated smiling Bodhisattva known as the Eastern Venus. Allow 1-1.5 hours. Ticket ~65 CNY. Book online for Labour Day holiday. Verified via RedNote (Huayan & Shanhua double temple guide, 179 likes).",
            "notes_local": "城区优先级1——大同古城全天步行游首站。中国最重要的辽代（916-1125年）佛教寺院之一。大雄宝殿是中国现存最大辽代佛殿；薄伽教藏楼（建于1038年）内有精美壁藏雕刻，以合掌露齿东方维纳斯菩萨像著称。游览约1-1.5小时，票价约65元，五一假期建议网上预约。小红书已验证（华严寺&善化寺双子星游记，179赞）。",
            "opening_hours": "08:30-17:30",
            "optional": false,
            "search_results": [
