          {
            "name_base": "Shanhua Temple (善化寺)",
            "name_local": "大同善化寺",
            "location_base": "Nansi Street, Ancient City Area, Datong, Shanxi",
            "location_local": "山西省大同市古城区南寺街",
            "coordinates": {
              "lat": 40.0862,
              "lng": 113.2935
            },
            "cost": 40,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Tang-liao-jin Dynasty Buddhist Temple",
            "type_local": "唐辽金代佛教寺院",
            "notes_base": "PRIORITY 2 city attraction — visit after Huayan Temple. One of China's best-preserved ancient temple complexes. Originally Tang dynasty, expanded Liao and Jin dynasties (10th-12th century). Contains four surviving Liao-Jin timber structures along a single central axis — the only site in China with all four — illustrating the full architectural transition from Tang to Jin styles. The Sansheng Hall and Great Hero Hall are highlights. Less crowded than Huayan. Allow 45-60 min. Ticket ~40 CNY. Described by RedNote users as a Liao-Jin architecture museum. Verified via RedNote (179 likes).",
            "notes_local": "城区优先级2——华严寺游览结束后前往。中国保存最完好的古代寺庙建筑群之一，始建于唐代，辽金时期（10-12世纪）扩建。沿中轴线保存有四座辽金木构建筑，是中国唯一一处集齐四座辽金木构的寺院，完整呈现从唐风到金代的建筑演变。三圣殿与大雄宝殿是参观重点，人少清净。游览约45-60分钟，票价约40元。小红书用户称其为辽金建筑博物馆，已验证（179赞）。",
            "opening_hours": "08:30-17:30",
            "optional": false,
            "search_results": [
              {
                "skill": "gaode-maps",
                "type": "geocode",
                "url": "https://uri.amap.com/marker?position=113.293500,40.086200&name=大同善化寺",
                "display_text": "Gaode Maps - Shanhua Temple Datong"
              },
