            "cost": 80,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Ming Dynasty Royal Palace",
            "type_local": "明代王府",
            "notes_base": "PRIORITY 3 — reconstructed Ming dynasty palace of Prince Zhu Guilei (Dai Wang), originally built 1374 AD. The Nine Dragon Screen (built 1392 AD) is the oldest and largest surviving nine-dragon glazed tile screen in China, predating Beijing's versions. Located ~5 min walk from Shanhua Temple. Ticket ~80 CNY. Allow 45-60 min. Focus on Nine Dragon Screen + main gate. Verified via RedNote (Datong Ancient City CityWalk guide, 1834 likes).",
            "notes_local": "城区优先级3——明代代王朱桂王府，始建于1374年，约2020年完成复原。宫殿前九龙壁（建于1392年）是中国现存最古老、最大的九龙琉璃照壁，比北京版本更早。距善化寺步行约5分钟，票价约80元，游览约45-60分钟。重点参观九龙壁与主仪门。小红书已验证（大同古城CityWalk攻略，1834赞）。",
            "opening_hours": "08:30-18:00 (peak season, last entry ~17:30)",
            "optional": false,
