        "location": "Chengdu",
        "attractions": [
          {
            "name_base": "Du Fu Thatched Cottage (杜甫草堂博物馆)",
            "name_local": "杜甫草堂博物馆",
            "location_base": "Caotang Road, Qingyang District, Chengdu, Sichuan",
            "location_local": "四川省成都市青羊区草堂路浣花溪历史文化风景区",
            "coordinates": {
              "lat": 30.660391,
              "lng": 104.030813
            },
            "cost": 50,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Historic Literary Shrine",
            "type_local": "历史文学圣地",
            "notes_base": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] Morning anchor. The most INFJ, literary, and historically resonant attraction in all of Chengdu. The actual thatched cottage of Tang dynasty poet Du Fu (杜甫), who wrote his most famous poems here during exile (759-762 AD). The site is now a vast museum-garden of bamboo groves, lotus ponds, memorial halls, and inscription stones. Recommended morning visit 08:30-11:30 (~3h) before crowds peak. Key stops: 工部祠 (Ministry Hall with Du Fu's statue), 少陵草堂碑亭 (Stone Stele Pavilion), bamboo corridors — INFJ visitors should sit in the bamboo grove and read. Ticket ~50 CNY. Pairs with nearby 浣花溪公园 (free). Verified via RedNote (清晨草堂美到失语: 2334 likes; 四川杜甫草堂: 1767 likes; 不绕路最全路线: 1169 likes; 万字图解攻略: 885 likes).",
            "notes_local": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] 早上主打。成都最具INFJ气质的文学圣地。唐代诗人杜甫流寓成都时（759-762年）实际居住的草堂，在此写下最著名诗篇。如今是竹林、荷塘、纪念殿堂和碑刻的博物馆式园林。建议8:30-11:30晨游（约3小时），趁人群未聚集。重点游览工部祠（杜甫塑像），少陵草堂碑亭，以及竹林走廊——INFJ游客可在竹林中静坐读诗。门票约50元，与旁边浣花溪公园（免费）衔接游览。小红书已验证（清晨杜甫草堂美到失语2334赞；四川杜甫草堂1767赞；不绕路最全路线1169赞；万字图解攻略885赞）。",
            "opening_hours": "08:00-18:00 (last entry 17:30)",
            "optional": false,
