            "type_base": "Literary Park",
            "type_local": "文学主题公园",
            "notes_base": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] Directly adjacent to Du Fu Cottage — the park is named after the creek (浣花溪) that flows past Du Fu's original dwelling, referenced in his poems. A free riverside park with weeping willows, stone bridges, and a large 成都诗歌节 (Chengdu Poetry Festival) venue. The setting is profoundly poetic in May when willows are green. Walk along the creek and through the bamboo grove from the Cottage exit gate as an extension of the morning visit (~45-60 min). Free entry.",
            "notes_local": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] 紧邻杜甫草堂，公园以流经草堂的浣花溪命名（杜甫诗中多次提及）。免费滨水公园，垂柳依依、石桥古朴，是成都诗歌节主会场。五月柳绿，意境极美。从草堂出口沿溪漫步穿行竹林，约需45-60分钟，与草堂完美衔接。免费入场。",
            "opening_hours": "06:00-22:00",
            "optional": false,
            "search_results": [
