            },
            "cost": 0,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Historic Temple",
            "type_local": "历史古寺",
            "notes_base": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] Morning start 10:00-11:30 (~1.5h). A Tang dynasty Buddhist monastery founded in 605 AD, famous as where the Tang monk Xuanzang (玄奘) studied before his westward journey to retrieve Buddhist scriptures. The temple sits dramatically inside the modern Taikoo Li complex, creating a powerful cultural contrast — ancient gilded eaves surrounded by glass boutiques. Free entry. The interior is tranquil with incense smoke, courtyard pines, and original Tang-dynasty layout. Particularly poetic in the morning before the shopping crowds arrive. The contrast with the surrounding luxury mall is its most striking 文艺 quality. Best visited first upon arriving at the 太古里 area, before the shopping energy takes over.",
            "notes_local": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] 上午10:00-11:30（约1.5小时）。始建于605年的唐代佛寺，著名的是玄奘法师西行取经前曾在此修习。古寺立于现代太古里购物区之中，形成极为强烈的文化对比——唐代金顶飞檐与玻璃精品店并存。免费入场。寺内香烟袅袅，庭院古松，唐代格局保留完整，早晨购物人群未至时最为宁静。抵达太古里后建议先游大慈寺，再漫步商业区。",
            "opening_hours": "08:00-17:30",
            "optional": false,
            "search_results": [
              {
                "skill": "gaode-maps",
                "type": "geocode",
                "url": "https://uri.amap.com/marker?position=104.080028,30.658194&name=大慈寺",
                "display_text": "Gaode Maps - Daci Monastery"
              }
            ]
