            },
            "cost": 0,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Open-Air Mixed-Use District",
            "type_local": "开放式商业文化区",
            "notes_base": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] Late morning 11:30-13:00 combined with Daci Monastery (~1.5h total for both). Despite its luxury mall status, the INFJ angle is the courtyard architecture and the hidden alleys (里弄) away from the main luxury shopping axis. The complex is built around the Daci Temple as its spiritual center, with interconnecting lanes of varying width, rooftop terraces, and courtyards. Key move: after visiting Daci Temple, walk the narrow 里弄 (alleyways) on the east and south sides of the complex — these have indie cafes, concept stores, and architectural moments rather than just luxury flagships. The entire complex is low-rise traditional-style architecture with eaves detail, deliberately designed to complement the Tang temple. Free to walk through. Connects directly to Chunxi Road on the north side.",
            "notes_local": "[PLAN A - PRIMARY] 上午晚段11:30-13:00与大慈寺合并游览（共约1.5小时）。虽是奢侈品购物区，INFJ视角在于其院落建筑与隐藏里弄。整个建筑群以大慈寺为精神核心，由宽窄不一的里弄连通，设有屋顶露台和院落。关键路线：游览大慈寺后，走建筑群东侧和南侧的窄里弄——独立咖啡馆、概念小店和建筑细节集中于此，而非奢侈品旗舰店。整体为低矮传统川派建筑风格，飞檐细节与唐代古寺相呼应。免费穿行。北侧直连春熙路。",
            "opening_hours": "Open 24 hours (shops 10:00-22:00)",
            "optional": false,
            "search_results": [
