          {
            "name_base": "Dujiangyan Irrigation System - UNESCO Water Engineering (都江堰水利工程)",
            "name_local": "都江堰景区",
            "location_base": "Dujiangyan Scenic Area, Dujiangyan City, Chengdu, Sichuan",
            "location_local": "四川省成都市都江堰市都江堰景区",
            "coordinates": {
              "lat": 31.003363,
              "lng": 103.610529
            },
            "cost": 80,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "UNESCO World Heritage Site",
            "type_local": "联合国教科文组织世界遗产",
            "notes_base": "[PLAN C - ALTERNATIVE] 都江堰 (Dujiangyan) — a 2,300-year-old hydraulic engineering system still in active use, UNESCO listed. Built by Li Bing in 256 BC, it divides the Min River into inner and outer channels using only natural water dynamics — no dam, no sluice gates. The system still irrigates 67 million people today. Key spots: Yuzui (Fish Mouth levee), Feishayan (Flying Sand Weir), Baopingkou (Bottle-Neck Channel). Walk the suspension bridge (Anlan Bridge) over the rushing Min River for atmospheric views. Ticket ~80 CNY. Allow 2.5-3 hours. Take HSR from Chengdu to Dujiangyan station (~30 min). Best combined with Guanxian Ancient City (灌县古城) afternoon walk.",
            "notes_local": "[PLAN C - ALTERNATIVE] 都江堰——公元前256年李冰父子建造的2300年历史水利工程，至今仍在使用，联合国教科文组织世界遗产。依靠纯粹的自然水动力将岷江分为内江和外江，无水坝无闸门，至今灌溉6700万人口。重点游览：鱼嘴、飞沙堰、宝瓶口；走安澜索桥横跨湍急岷江，体验感十足。门票约80元，游览需2.5-3小时。乘成都→都江堰高铁约30分钟。建议下午前往灌县古城漫步搭配。",
            "opening_hours": "08:00-18:30 (peak season)",
            "optional": true,
            "search_results": [
              {
                "skill": "gaode-maps",
                "type": "geocode",
                "url": "https://uri.amap.com/marker?position=103.610529,31.003363&name=都江堰景区",
                "display_text": "Gaode Maps - Dujiangyan Scenic Area"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name_base": "Guanxian Ancient City Walk (灌县古城)",
            "name_local": "灌县古城",
            "location_base": "Dujiangyan City, Chengdu, Sichuan",
            "location_local": "四川省成都市都江堰市灌县古城",
            "coordinates": {
              "lat": 30.998567,
              "lng": 103.620012
            },
            "cost": 0,
            "currency_local": "CNY",
            "type_base": "Historic Ancient Town",
            "type_local": "历史古城",
            "notes_base": "[PLAN C - ALTERNATIVE] Directly adjacent to Dujiangyan Scenic Area — the ancient city of Guanxian (灌县古城) is the old county town center with Qing dynasty architecture, a stone-paved main street, a preserved city gate tower, and a riverfront promenade along the Min River. Far less crowded than Dujiangyan scenic area itself. Excellent for post-Dujiangyan afternoon stroll. Key spot: Nan Bridge (南桥) — a covered ornamental bridge over the Min River with intricate paintings and carvings, one of Dujiangyan's most photographed landmarks. Free. Allow 1-1.5 hours.",
            "notes_local": "[PLAN C - ALTERNATIVE] 紧邻都江堰景区——灌县古城是老县城中心，有清代建筑、青石板主街、保存完整的城门楼和岷江滨河步道。比都江堰景区人少很多，适合下午漫步。重点：南桥——横跨岷江的彩绘装饰廊桥，雕梁画栋，是都江堰最具代表性的拍照地之一。免费参观，建议游览1-1.5小时。",
            "opening_hours": "Open 24 hours (outdoor town)",
            "optional": true,
            "search_results": [
